and $v \in \R_j$, $i<j$. 
We say $v$ is reachable from $u$ (or $u$ can reach  $v$), 
if a semi-feasible curve $R$ exists 
which ends at point $v$ and visits $u$.
Furthermore, we say point $u$ can directly reach  $v$,
if $u$ is a reachable point and $u$
